	"Release-triggering changes require non-empty bumps",
);
expect((failure as Error).message).toContain(
	"cloudflare.config.ts -> @hevy-mcp/worker",
);
```

That asserts the specific failure mode (empty changeset cannot accompany a worker-triggering change; requires non-empty worker bump) rather than the ambiguous substring. Note the test name says "requires a Worker release" — the message "Release-triggering changes require non-empty bumps" + mapping covers it.

Hmm — one question: should this scenario instead produce the "need a changeset" error? The original intent (from the ORIGINAL test, which also wrote an empty changeset): empty changeset + worker config change → error. The current behavior: empty-changeset error. Keeping behavior, asserting the exact reason. Good.

